{"name":"Young Crab","hex":"#f6a09d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"young","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["In the early part of growth or life; born not long ago.","At an early stage of existence or development; having recently come into existence."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Offspring, especially the immature offspring of animals."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/young"},{"term":"crab","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any crustacean of the infraorder Brachyura, having five pairs of legs, the foremost of which are in the form of claws, and a carapace.","The meat of this crustacean, served as food; crabmeat."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fish for crabs.","To ruin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crab"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crab","blocks":[{"text":"Crabs are decapod crustaceans, either the Brachyura or various groups within the closely related Anomura, characterised by having a heavily armoured shell, their tail segments concealed under the body, the ability to run sideways, and the habit of hiding in rocky crevices. They do not form a single natural group or clade, but have convergently evolved multiple times from the ancestral decapod body plan through carcinisation, the process of creating this set of characteristics. As a group, they are thus polyphyletic, meaning they have multiple evolutionary origins."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Cancer_pagurus.jpg/330px-Cancer_pagurus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crab"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Horseshoe_crab_%28white_background%29.jpg/500px-Horseshoe_crab_%28white_background%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Horseshoe_crab_%28white_background%29